{#- The EDLC loop (paper, Figure 1): ten stages clockwise from twelve o'clock, the operate half
    (9–10) drawn dashed, and the feedback path from Improve back to the design stages. The arrow is drawn
    towards Specify, but the paper leaves the re-entry point open, so the <desc> names no stage.
    Each node is a link to its stage page, in stage order for the keyboard, named "Stage n, Name".
    The svg is a group, not an image, so its links stay reachable by assistive technology. Positions
    come from `_data/stages.js`; the ordered list beneath carries the same content for readers who do
    not see the figure. Long names wrap onto two lines so the labels stay inside a tight viewBox centred
    on the circle. -#}
<figure class="loop">
  <svg viewBox="-80 0 680 520" role="group" aria-labelledby="loop-title" aria-describedby="loop-desc">
    <title id="loop-title">The Education Development Lifecycle loop</title>
    <desc id="loop-desc">Ten stages in a circle. Stages 1 to 8 design and release a program; stages 9 and 10 operate it. An arrow from stage 10, Improve, returns to the design stages. Each stage links to its page.</desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="loop-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="loop__arrowhead"/>
      </marker>
    </defs>
    <g aria-hidden="true">
      <circle cx="260" cy="260" r="190" class="loop__track"/>
      {%- set improve = stages | stageByNumber(10) -%}
      {%- set specify = stages | stageByNumber(2) -%}
      <path d="M{{ improve.x + 18 }},{{ improve.y + 22 }} Q260,250 {{ specify.x - 30 }},{{ specify.y + 20 }}" class="loop__feedback" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)"/>
      <text x="260" y="232" class="loop__note" text-anchor="middle">What delivery teaches</text>
      <text x="260" y="250" class="loop__note" text-anchor="middle">returns to design</text>
    </g>
    {%- for s in stages %}
    {%- set right = s.x > 262 -%}
    {%- set mid = s.x >= 258 and s.x <= 262 -%}
    {%- set words = s.name.split(" ") -%}
    {%- set wrap = s.name.length > 13 and words.length > 1 -%}
    {%- set lx = s.x if mid else (s.x + 40 if right else s.x - 40) -%}
    {%- set ly = (s.y - 42) if (mid and s.y < 260) else ((s.y + 54) if mid else (s.y + 6)) -%}
    <a href="{{ s.url | url }}" class="loop__node loop__node--{{ s.half }}" aria-label="Stage {{ s.n }}, {{ s.name }}">
      <circle cx="{{ s.x }}" cy="{{ s.y }}" r="38" class="loop__focus"/>
      <circle cx="{{ s.x }}" cy="{{ s.y }}" r="30" class="loop__dot"/>
      <text x="{{ s.x }}" y="{{ s.y + 7 }}" text-anchor="middle" class="loop__num">{{ s.n }}</text>
      <text x="{{ lx }}" y="{{ (ly - 10) if wrap else ly }}" text-anchor="{{ 'middle' if mid else ('start' if right else 'end') }}" class="loop__label">
        {%- if wrap -%}
        <tspan x="{{ lx }}">{{ words.slice(0, -1).join(" ") }}</tspan><tspan x="{{ lx }}" dy="1.2em">{{ words | last }}</tspan>
        {%- else -%}
        {{ s.name }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </text>
    </a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    <ol class="loop__list">
      {%- for s in stages %}
      <li><a href="{{ s.url | url }}">{{ s.name }}</a><span> — {{ s.question }}</span></li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
